# AI-SDLC MCP Agents (Jira & GitHub Orchestrators)

Autonomous AI-SDLC workflows built on the **Model Context Protocol (MCP v2.x)** and **Google Gemini (`langchain-google-genai`)**. Each domain uses its own dedicated MCP server and standalone orchestrator over `stdio`:
1. **Jira Workflow (`ai_orchestrator.py` + `jira_mcp_server.py`)**: Discovers 5 Jira REST API v3 tools to list, create, update, comment on, and transition tickets in project **`CP`**.
2. **GitHub PR Workflow (`github_orchestrator.py` + `github_mcp_server.py`)**: Discovers 6 GitHub REST API tools to inspect files, search code, create feature branches, commit code updates, and raise Pull Requests in **`pavi550/Capstone`**.

---

## 1. Directory Structure (`Capstone/mcp/`)

```text
Capstone/
└── mcp/
    ├── jira_mcp_server.py        # MCP v2.x server exposing 5 Jira REST API v3 tools
    ├── ai_orchestrator.py        # Standalone Jira orchestrator powered by Gemini
    ├── github_mcp_server.py      # MCP v2.x server exposing 6 GitHub REST API tools
    ├── github_orchestrator.py    # Standalone GitHub PR orchestrator powered by Gemini
    └── README.md                 # Complete setup, configuration, and run guide
```

---

## 2. Architecture Flow

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐         stdio (JSON-RPC)         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│      ai_orchestrator.py     │ ◄──────────────────────────────► │      jira_mcp_server.py     │
│   (Standalone Jira Agent)   │   5 Jira Tools (list, create,    │  capstoneprojectgrp4 (CP)   │
└─────────────────────────────┘   update, comment, transition)   └─────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────┐         stdio (JSON-RPC)         ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│    github_orchestrator.py   │ ◄──────────────────────────────► │     github_mcp_server.py    │
│  (Standalone GitHub Agent)  │   6 GitHub Tools (list, search,  │      pavi550/Capstone       │
└─────────────────────────────┘   read, branch, commit, PR)      └─────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Prerequisites & Installation

- **Python**: 3.10 or higher (tested on Python 3.13 on Windows / Git Bash)
- **Google AI Studio API Key**: Active key (`AIza...`) from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
- **Atlassian Jira API Token**: Active token from [Atlassian Security Settings](https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens)
- **GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)**: Active token scoped to `pavi550/Capstone`

Install required Python dependencies:

```bash
pip install "mcp>=2.0.0" langchain-core langchain-google-genai requests
```

---

## 4. Credentials & Environment Variables

Both MCP servers validate credentials immediately at startup and read secrets from environment variables so no tokens are hardcoded or committed to Git.

### Required Token Scopes
- **Google Gemini (`GOOGLE_API_KEY`)**: Standard Gemini API key (`AIza...`).
- **Atlassian Jira (`JIRA_API_TOKEN`)**: API token for `pes2pge25ds030@stu.pes.edu` with access to project `CP` on `https://capstoneprojectgrp4.atlassian.net`.
- **GitHub (`GITHUB_TOKEN`)**:
  - **Fine-grained PAT** (scoped to `pavi550/Capstone`): `Contents: Read and write`, `Pull requests: Read and write`, `Metadata: Read-only`.
  - **Classic PAT**: `repo` scope.

### Export Variables in Terminal (Git Bash)

```bash
export GOOGLE_API_KEY="AIzaSyYourActualGoogleAIStudioKey"
export JIRA_API_TOKEN="your_atlassian_jira_api_token"
export GITHUB_TOKEN="your_github_personal_access_token"
export GITHUB_OWNER="pavi550"
export GITHUB_REPO="Capstone"
export GITHUB_BRANCH="main"
```

*(For Windows PowerShell, use `$env:GOOGLE_API_KEY="..."`, `$env:JIRA_API_TOKEN="..."`, `$env:GITHUB_TOKEN="..."`, etc.)*

### Quick Pre-Flight Checks
```bash
# 1. Verify Google API Key
curl -s "[https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=$GOOGLE_API_KEY](https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=$GOOGLE_API_KEY)" | head -n 5

# 2. Verify Jira Auth & Project CP
curl -s -u "pes2pge25ds030@stu.pes.edu:$JIRA_API_TOKEN" "[https://capstoneprojectgrp4.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/project/CP](https://capstoneprojectgrp4.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/project/CP)" | grep '"key"'

# 3. Verify GitHub Repo Access & Default Branch
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN" "[https://api.github.com/repos/$GITHUB_OWNER/$GITHUB_REPO](https://api.github.com/repos/$GITHUB_OWNER/$GITHUB_REPO)" | grep -E '"full_name"|"default_branch"'
```

---

## 5. Script Configuration Summary

### A. Jira Scripts (`jira_mcp_server.py` & `ai_orchestrator.py`)
- **`DOMAIN` & `EMAIL`**: Configured for `https://capstoneprojectgrp4.atlassian.net` and `pes2pge25ds030@stu.pes.edu`.
- **Token Guard**: `jira_mcp_server.py` raises a `RuntimeError` at startup if `JIRA_API_TOKEN` is unset or still set to `"YOUR_ACTIVE_JIRA_TOKEN"`.
- **Path & Model Resilience**: `ai_orchestrator.py` resolves `jira_mcp_server.py` dynamically via `os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))` and uses `gemini-3.8-flash` with a `gemini-3.8-pro` fallback.
- **Customizing Tasks**: Edit the `prompt` variable inside `ai_orchestrator.py` to specify which `CP` tickets to create, update, comment on, or transition.

### B. GitHub Scripts (`github_mcp_server.py` & `github_orchestrator.py`)
- **Token Guard**: `github_mcp_server.py` raises a `RuntimeError` at startup if `GITHUB_TOKEN` or `GITHUB_OWNER` is missing.
- **Branch Safety Guard**: `commit_file_change` blocks direct commits to `main`/`master`, requiring Gemini to create a feature branch via `create_branch` first.
- **Automatic Blob SHA Resolution**: Automatically fetches the existing file's SHA when modifying an existing file so both new file creation (`HTTP 201`) and updates (`HTTP 200`) work seamlessly.
- **Timeout Resilience**: `github_orchestrator.py` uses `timeout=120` and `max_retries=2` across `gemini-3.8-flash` and `gemini-3.8-pro` to prevent `504 DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` during full-file code generation.
- **Customizing Tasks**: Edit the `prompt` variable inside `github_orchestrator.py` to specify what code changes Gemini should implement and PR.

---

## 6. How to Start Each Orchestrator

> **Important:** Do **not** run `jira_mcp_server.py` or `github_mcp_server.py` manually. Each orchestrator automatically launches its respective MCP server as a background subprocess over `stdio`, discovers its tools, runs the workflow, and terminates the child process on exit.

### Workflow 1: Run the Jira Orchestrator (`ai_orchestrator.py`)
From `~/Capstone` (or `~/Capstone/mcp`):
```bash
cd ~/Capstone
python -u mcp/ai_orchestrator.py
```

**Expected Output:**
```text
🔌 Connected! Gemini dynamically learned 5 tools via MCP.

🤖 Gemini is thinking and orchestrating the workflow...

   ⚙️ Gemini decided to execute MCP Tool: create_jira_ticket
   ⚙️ Gemini decided to execute MCP Tool: list_open_jiras

✅ Final AI Project Manager Report:
...
```

### Workflow 2: Run the GitHub PR Orchestrator (`github_orchestrator.py`)
From `~/Capstone` (or `~/Capstone/mcp`):
```bash
cd ~/Capstone
python -u mcp/github_orchestrator.py
```

**Expected Output:**
```text
🔌 Connected to GitHub MCP Server! Learned 6 tools.

🤖 Gemini is inspecting pavi550/Capstone and preparing a PR...

   ⚙️ Gemini executing MCP Tool: list_repo_files
   ⚙️ Gemini executing MCP Tool: read_file
   ⚙️ Gemini executing MCP Tool: create_branch
   ⚙️ Gemini executing MCP Tool: commit_file_change
   ⚙️ Gemini executing MCP Tool: create_pull_request

✅ Final GitHub PR Agent Report:
... (includes direct URL to the newly opened Pull Request)
```

*(Always pass `-u` so Python streams `asyncio` tool execution logs in real time.)*

---

## 7. Available MCP Tools Reference

### Jira MCP Tools (`jira_mcp_server.py` — 5 Tools)
| Tool Name | Parameters | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `list_open_jiras` | `project_key="CP"` | Lists all open (non-Done) Jira tickets and their current statuses. |
| `create_jira_ticket` | `summary`, `description`, `project_key="CP"`, `issue_type="Task"` | Creates a new Jira ticket formatted in Atlassian Document Format (ADF). |
| `update_jira_fields` | `issue_key`, `summary=""`, `description=""` | Updates the title and/or description of an existing ticket (e.g., `CP-2`). |
| `add_jira_comment` | `issue_key`, `comment_text` | Posts review notes, logs, or PR links onto an existing ticket. |
| `update_jira_status` | `issue_key`, `target_status` | Resolves workflow transition IDs and moves a ticket (`To Do` → `In Progress` → `Done`). |

### GitHub MCP Tools (`github_mcp_server.py` — 6 Tools)
| Tool Name | Parameters | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `list_repo_files` | `branch="main"`, `path_prefix=""`, `extension=".java"` | Lists repository files via GitHub Git Trees API. Pass `extension=""` to list all file types. |
| `search_repo_code` | `keyword` | Searches across `pavi550/Capstone` for classes, methods, or keywords. |
| `read_file` | `file_path`, `branch="main"`, `start_line=1`, `end_line=300` | Fetches and decodes source files with line numbers for code comprehension. |
| `create_branch` | `new_branch_name`, `base_branch="main"` | Cuts a new feature branch from the latest commit SHA of the base branch. |
| `commit_file_change` | `file_path`, `updated_full_content`, `commit_message`, `branch` | Creates or updates a file on a feature branch (auto-resolves existing file SHA; blocks direct commits to `main`). |
| `create_pull_request` | `title`, `body`, `head_branch`, `base_branch="main"` | Raises a Pull Request on GitHub and returns the PR number and HTML URL. |

---

## 8. Troubleshooting

| Error / Symptom | Cause | Resolution |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `RuntimeError: CRITICAL: JIRA_API_TOKEN is not updated` | `JIRA_API_TOKEN` is unset or still a placeholder. | Export `JIRA_API_TOKEN` in your current shell before starting `ai_orchestrator.py`. |
| `RuntimeError: CRITICAL: GITHUB_TOKEN and GITHUB_OWNER must be set` | `GITHUB_TOKEN` or `GITHUB_OWNER` is missing. | Export `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GITHUB_OWNER="pavi550"` before starting `github_orchestrator.py`. |
| `ToolError: Jira Authentication Failed (HTTP 401/403)` | Jira token expired or lacks project `CP` permissions. | Generate a new token in Atlassian Account Settings and re-export. |
| `ToolError: GitHub Auth/Permission Error (HTTP 401/403)` | GitHub PAT expired or lacks `Contents` / `Pull requests` write access. | Regenerate PAT with write permissions (or classic `repo` scope). |
| `ToolError: GitHub Not Found (404)` | Branch mismatch (`main` vs `master`) or invalid file path. | Run the GitHub `curl` check in Section 4 to verify `"default_branch"`. |
| `400 INVALID_ARGUMENT (API_KEY_INVALID)` | `GOOGLE_API_KEY` is missing, malformed, or revoked. | Generate a fresh `AIza...` key in Google AI Studio and re-export. |
| `504 DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` | Generating full code files exceeded the LLM request timeout. | Ensure `timeout=120` is set on `ChatGoogleGenerativeAI` in `github_orchestrator.py`. |
| `503 UNAVAILABLE` from Gemini | Temporary demand spike on `gemini-3.8-flash`. | Keep `.with_fallbacks([fallback_llm])` configured with `gemini-3.8-pro`. |
